# PR-first delivery after every task

The delivery law has one home: **`AGENTS.md` §5.1** (clean start, mandatory finish, head deletion, clean tree). This file does not restate it (ADR 051). The gates are MUST; casual phrasing never waives them; only an explicit user override does, stated in the PR body.

- **Start:** `git fetch origin`, a new focused branch from `origin/master`, never on a dirty tree.
- **Finish:** verify, `git add <paths>` (never `-A`, never `stash`), commit, push, open a **ready (non-draft)** PR from `.github/pull_request_template.md`. The PR URL is the finish line. Actions merges it (`github-delivery.mdc`).
- **After merge or close:** delete the head the same session (`github-delivery.mdc` item 8; `branch-cleanup.mdc` for tips not in master).

## Deploy

- **Backend has no cloud host** (local / Desktop sidecar only). Pushing git does not deploy the API. Do not assume Railway or another PaaS.
- **Public site** is not in this repo: `nova.altaystudio.com` is built from `aaltaay/nova-site`.
- **Supabase** edge functions or schemas changed? Deploy them with the `supabase` tool / CLI.
- A deploy script in `package.json` / `Makefile` / docs? Run it. Target unclear? Check `AGENTS.md` §8 / `README.md` or ask.
- Report the deploy status, including "no backend cloud deploy" when only local applies.
